Targets: wasm
Subject: Provide System V shared memory calls for a single-process WebAssembly build
Purpose: Emscripten has no shmget/shmat/shmdt/shmctl, but the server calls them at startup (the small interlock segment next to the anonymous main segment, and the dynamic shared memory control segment). A WebAssembly server is one process, so a segment is a block of the process's own memory. This file implements exactly the calls and the shmid_ds fields PostgreSQL uses, in-process, and only when __EMSCRIPTEN__ is defined; other builds compile an empty unit.
Components: src/backend/port/wasm_shm.c (new), src/backend/port/Makefile
Checks: scripts/build-wasm.sh links postgres with no undefined symbols; postgres --boot and --single start under node (scripts/test-wasm-node.sh)
Origin: own
Ported-from: 13.23 (wasm/0001-wasm-shared-memory.patch) for 12.22 by scripts/port-patches.js
Ported-from: 12.22 (wasm/pg12/0001-wasm-shared-memory.patch) for 11.22 by scripts/port-patches.js
